  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Isoleucine -&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0059_216400fa910f.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p>Isoleucine is a neutral amino acid.</p><p>Cysteine -&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0059_4103c23b2f5a.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 133px;\" /></p><p>Cysteine is a sulphur containing amino acid. It contain thiol group.</p><p>Lysine -&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0059_a623f5e49769.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 173px;\" /></p><p>Lysine is a basic amino acid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Methionine -&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0059_870a3c8fa748.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 191px;\" /></p><p>Methionine is a sulphur containing amino acid contain thioether group.</p><p>Glutamic acid -&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0059_123fa332a833.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 185px;\" /></p><p>Glutamic acid is an acidic amino acid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>"
